      "heading": "Safeguarding across the UK",
      "html": "<p>The law differs. In England the Care Act 2014 puts duties on local authorities, and providers work within local arrangements. In Scotland the Adult Support and Protection (Scotland) Act 2007 applies. Wales and Northern Ireland have their own.</p><p>Everywhere, a home must spot concerns, raise them at once and keep a record.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
